# Local CI gate — scoped at commit · full before push

Two tiers:

| Tier | When | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| **Scoped gate** | Orchestrator **execution commits** and **verification (Layer 2)** only | Packages derived from staged/committed paths only |
| **Full gate** | Immediately before **`git push`** to any remote | Entire workspace (Turborepo) |

## Who runs what

| Workflow | Before commit | Before push |
|---|---|---|
| **Direct / interactive agent** (user says commit, commit and push, etc. — **not** an orchestrator sub-agent) | **No CI gate** — commit after staging explicit paths | **Full gate only** (once; do not run scoped gate first) |
| **Orchestrator sub-agents** (execution + verification) | **Scoped gate** on touched packages | **Full gate** only when user/orchestrator explicitly requests push (PUSH PREP) |

**Direct commit and push:** run the full gate **once**, immediately before `git push`. Do **not** run a scoped gate before the commit — that would duplicate work.

Orchestrated sub-agents: see `.cursor/skills/orchestrator/SKILL.md` and `prompt-templates.md` (SCOPED CI GATE block).

## Gate trigger: code-impacting changes only

These paths determine whether CI gates apply. **Which gate** depends on the workflow table above.

When staged changes are in directories/files exercised by CI commands:

- `packages/**`
- `apps/**`
- `e2e/**`
- `infra/**`
- `scripts/**`
- `.github/scripts/**`

Also apply when these shared root files are staged:

- `package.json`
- `pnpm-lock.yaml`
- `pnpm-workspace.yaml`
- `turbo.json` (if present)

For root workspace files: orchestrator sub-agents run scoped gate on implementation packages in the commit plus **full gate before push**; direct agents skip scoped gate and run **full gate before push** only.

## Non-code changes (scoped/full gate not required)

Skip scoped and full gates when staged changes are only in:

- `docs/**`, `*.md`
- `.cursor/**` (rules, skills, memory files)
- `.github/workflows/**`
- Other repo metadata that does not affect shipped runtime code

For these commits, run **targeted validation only** (e.g. YAML parse for workflow edits) and report that CI gates were intentionally skipped.

## Scoped gate (orchestrator sub-agents only)

**Orchestrator execution agents** before implementation commit and **verification agents** at Layer 2. **Not** used for direct/interactive commits (user says commit or commit and push without orchestrator dispatch).

Derive `--filter` from touched paths (staged paths for commit; committed paths for verify).

### Path → filter mapping

| Path prefix | pnpm filter |
|---|---|
| `packages/backend/` | `@slugbase/backend` |
| `packages/web/` | `@slugbase/web` |
| `packages/marketing/` | `@slugbase/marketing` |
| `packages/ui/` | `@slugbase/ui` |
| `packages/shared-types/` | `@slugbase/shared-types` |
| `packages/db-admin/` | `@slugbase/db-admin` |
| `packages/admin/` | `@slugbase/admin` |
| `packages/email-templates/` | `@slugbase/email-templates` |
| `apps/**` | map to matching `@slugbase/*` if present |

### Filter suffix rules

- App/package-only change → `--filter @slugbase/<pkg>`
- Contract package (`shared-types`, `ui`) → `--filter @slugbase/<pkg>...` (include downstream consumers)
- Multiple packages in one task → union filters or repeat commands per package

### Commands

**Always** use the repo Node bootstrap (`bash scripts/with-ci-env.sh`) so marketing/Astro runs on Node >=22.12 (not Cursor's bundled Node 20):

```bash
bash scripts/with-ci-env.sh pnpm turbo run lint typecheck test:unit build --filter=@slugbase/<pkg>
# integration only when that package defines test:integration and the task warrants it:
bash scripts/with-ci-env.sh pnpm turbo run test:integration --filter=@slugbase/backend
```

Mark a command `n/a` only when a package legitimately has no such task yet — never to skip a defined check.

### Root-level extras (not turbo-filtered)

- Locale JSON touched → `pnpm i18n:validate` (+ `pnpm i18n:codegen` if en key set changed)
- Marketing blog content → `pnpm blog:validate`
- `scripts/**` or `e2e/**` touched → include filters for affected packages or run relevant root scripts from the plan Tests column

### Scoped gate enforcement

- If any scoped-gate command fails, **do not commit** (execution) or mark verifier **FAIL**.
- **Do not** run the full workspace gate before commit to substitute for scoped failures.
- **Do not** run scoped commands without `--filter` (that runs the full workspace accidentally).

## Full gate

**Mandatory immediately before `git push`** to any remote (typically `staging`; never `main` per `01-git-workflow.mdc`).

**Separate from the version bump gate:** `.githooks/pre-push` runs `check-push-version-bumps.mjs` automatically on push to `staging`/`main`. Fix failures with `pnpm bump:versions` (rule `15-deploy-version-bumps.mdc`). Recommended order before push:

1. `pnpm bump:versions` → commit `package.json` (when deploy code changed)
2. Full CI gate (below)
3. `git push`

- **Direct commit and push:** full gate is the only manual CI gate — do not run scoped gate before commit.
- **Orchestrator sub-agents:** run scoped gate at commit/verify; run full gate only when push is explicitly requested.
- **Commit without push (direct):** full gate not required until a later push.

When pushing code-impacting work, run (via Turborepo across the workspace):

```bash
bash scripts/with-ci-env.sh pnpm lint && \
bash scripts/with-ci-env.sh pnpm typecheck && \
bash scripts/with-ci-env.sh pnpm test:unit && \
bash scripts/with-ci-env.sh pnpm build && \
bash scripts/with-ci-env.sh pnpm test:integration && \
bash scripts/with-ci-env.sh pnpm audit --audit-level=high
```

Quick sanity check: `pnpm env:check` (see `docs/internal/local-development.md`).

**Stack note (settled — spec §19):** `lint`/`typecheck`/`test:unit`/`build`/`test:integration` are root Turborepo tasks fanning out to `backend` (NestJS), `web` (React Router v7), `marketing` (Astro), `shared-types`, and `ui`. Unit/integration use **Vitest** (+ Supertest for the API). **Playwright e2e is not part of the local gate** — it runs only on the `staging → main` PR in CI (spec §22.4). If a package legitimately has no task yet, mark that command `n/a` and note it; do not invent skips for code-impacting changes.

### Full gate enforcement

- If any full-gate command fails, **do not push**. Fix failures first, then rerun from the start.
- After a successful pre-push full gate, explicitly report that the full gate passed.
- Do not skip the full gate before push because failures are "likely unrelated".

## Critical: integration tests must NOT use the Phase wrapper

**Never** run `pnpm test:integration` wrapped with `phase run --`:

```bash
# ❌ WRONG — injects env vars that break integration tests
phase run -- pnpm test:integration

# ✅ CORRECT — integration script uses its own validTestEnv
pnpm test:integration
```

**Why:** The integration test script uses `validTestEnv` with boolean literals. Wrapping `pnpm test:integration` with Phase can still override those vars with string values and change runtime behavior. Backend deployment booleans use `envBoolean()` in `env.schema.ts` so Phase `"false"` parses correctly at app startup — but keep integration off Phase to avoid env pollution during tests.

**Rule:** `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test:unit`, and `pnpm build` may be run with `phase run --` when secrets are required (wrap via `bash scripts/with-ci-env.sh phase run -- pnpm …`). `pnpm test:integration` must always be run **without** the Phase wrapper (still use `with-ci-env.sh` for Node only).

This applies to **orchestrator sub-agents** (scoped pre-commit gate, scoped Layer 2) and **pre-push** full gate runs (all workflows).
